            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "The biggest activist battles of 2025",
            "description": "<p>Activist investing has surged on Wall Street this year. <br><br>There were 61 new campaigns launched in the third quarter, according to Barclays. That marks an increase from the second quarter, when 60 campaigns were launched, and a dramatic jump from a year ago, when activists launched just 36 fights. The most active activist is probably billionaire Paul Singer, whose Elliott Management manages $76 billion as of the end of June. But it\u2019s not just Elliott. Yahoo Finance Anchors <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/\">Julie Hyman</a> and <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> take a look at the rise of activist investing, the key players to know and the companies facing the most pressure.</p>\n<p>For full interviews, highlights, and key insights, check out more from\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/topic/yf-invest/\">Yahoo Finance Invest</a>.</p>",
